    "title": "Indian techie who lived and worked in the US for over 10 years shares what made him move back | Trending",
    "text": "H-1B visa struggles\nImmigration uncertainty was another major factor. Ravi, who was on an H-1B visa, pointed to the long green card backlog for Indians. “If your goal is to get a green card, the current wait time is around 150 to 190 years,” he said bluntly, adding that he would not recommend moving to the US if permanent settlement is the goal. He also spoke about being treated like a “temporary worker” and experiencing “subtle, silent discrimination”.",
